Sun Mar 23 2025  Lee Noar  <lee.noar@sky.com>

	Remove use of virtual method table, improve destruction of IPC and file objects to 
	prevent memory leaks
	* opentable.{h/c}(struct opentable_entry): Remove. A virtual method table is perhaps
	  a bit overkill; revert to using object type and switch statements.
	  (opentable_deref_mmap): Remove. Having two methods that do the same thing, but with
	  different parameter type (the other being opentable_deref_entry), is confusing and
	  error prone. Make it so we we only need opentable_deref_entry.
	  (opentable_log): Use switch instead of virtual method table.
	* filetable.{h/c}: Remove usage of virtual method table.
	  (systemfiletable_deref_entry): Change parameter to open table pointer so that we
	  have access to the file mapping if there is one and can then release the memory.
	  (systemfiletable_deref_file): Remove in favour of using systemfiletable_deref_file
	  instead.
	  (opentable_log_file_entry): Change visibility from static to extern.
	  (struct openfiletable): Add a mapping so that if the file is mmapped, we know where
	  and can release the memory in future.
	* shmtable.{h/c}(systemshmtable_deref_shm): Remove in favour of using systemshmtable_deref_entry
	  instead.
	  Remove usage of virtual method table.
	  (opentable_log_shm_entry): Change visibility from static to extern.
	* ipctable.{h/c}(struct systemipctable_entry): Add members to store the address and size
	  of the mmapped shared object. When destroying the IPC object, we have to munmap the memory
	  to ensure all the correct house keeping is performed, e.g., reference counting, etc.
	  Remove usage of virtual method table.
	  (opentable_add_ipc): Record buffer start and size.
	  (systemipctable_deref_ipc): Use munmap rather than opentable_deref_entry to ensure that
	  everything is kept in sync (e.g., the application specific mapping).
	  (opentable_unmap_ipc): Remove in favour of using systemipctable_deref_ipc instead.
	  (systemipctable_mmap): New method to ensure that when an IPC FD is passed to this app,
	  either at process start up or via IPC itself (see ipcop_read_fds), that the buffer is
	  is made known to this app by mmapping it in.
	  (opentable_log_ipc_entry): Change visibility from static to extern.
	* fdtable.c(fdtable_copy): If we're copying an IPC FD, then map its buffer into this app
	  so that it's destroyed correctly in future.
	* ipcop.c(ipcop_read_fds): If we're receiving an IPC FD, then map its buffer into this app
	  so that it's destroyed correctly in future.
	* main.c(app_new): Move the initialisation of the mmap_table array to earlier on so that
	  fdtable_copy can use armeabi_mmap.
	* mmap.{h/c}(armeabi_mmap): Make sure we NULL the returned address if there's an error.
	  (map_in_IPC): New method that takes an IPC open table entry and increments the reference
	  count for the shared memory object and adds the buffer memory to the application mappings.
	  (armeabi_mmap_internal): Only recognise a file mapping if the offset and size are also a
	  match.
	  Check for an IPC object and use map_in_IPC.
	  If a new file mapping is detected, then record it in the file object.
	  (armeabi_munmap): Use switch statement instead of virtual method table.
	  (appmmap_get_mapping_by_opentable_idx): New method to find an app mapping that references
	  a particular open table entry.
	  (mmap_allocator_pool_dump): New debug method to display the linked list of memory allocations
	  with an allocator.

